---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PolicyContact from "../components/PolicyContact.astro";
import { THEME_STORAGE_KEY } from "../lib/keys";
import { LEGAL_HOLDER } from "../data/site";
---

<Layout
  title="The Bead Reserve : Privacy"
  description="What The Bead Reserve's website collects and what it keeps in the browser."
>
  <main>
    <article class="policy bracket-frame">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Last updated: October 8, 2026</p>
        <p>
          This policy covers the website of The Bead Reserve, operated by
          {LEGAL_HOLDER}. The site has no accounts. It collects very little.
        </p>

        <h2>What the site collects</h2>
        <p>
          The site is hosted by
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/">Cloudflare</a>. Like nearly
          every host, Cloudflare may keep standard request logs as part of
          serving the site. A log entry includes the requesting IP address and
          the page requested.
        </p>
        <p>
          The camera frames and reserve status on the home page are served by
          the Reserve's own Worker, at <code>/api/</code> on this domain.
          Requests for them are ordinary requests to this site and are covered
          by the paragraph above.
        </p>
        <p>
          The site uses
          <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/"
            >Cloudflare Web Analytics</a
          >
          to count page views. Cloudflare adds a small script to each page for
          this. It sets no cookies, stores nothing in the browser, and does not
          follow a visitor to other sites. It produces a tally of which pages
          were read.
        </p>
        <p>
          The typefaces are served from this site. No font is requested from a
          third party.
        </p>
        <p>
          Claiming and redeeming BEADZ connect a wallet to the site. The site
          reads the wallet's public address to show its holdings and to submit
          the transaction the holder approves. The site does not store the
          address. Transactions on Base are public and permanent. The Reserve
          can neither hide nor remove them.
        </p>
        <p>
          A redemption is delivered by certified mail, which requires a name and
          a postal address. These are collected at redemption, used to address
          that shipment and nothing else, and deleted once delivery is
          confirmed.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
        <p>
          The site sets no cookies of its own. Cloudflare runs bot protection in
          front of the site, and that sets one cookie, <code>cf_clearance</code
          >. It records that the browser has already passed Cloudflare's check,
          so the browser is not challenged again. It lasts up to a year. Only
          Cloudflare can read it. It is not used for advertising or for tracking
          across sites.
        </p>
        <p>
          The site also keeps two small values in the browser's local storage.
          Neither is sent anywhere. Neither identifies anyone.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <code>{THEME_STORAGE_KEY}</code>: the light or dark theme choice,
            saved when the theme toggle is used.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>half-built-ecosystem</code>: a copy of the footer's list of
            related sites, kept for a day so it is not fetched on every page.
            The list comes from ecosystem.half-built-robots.com, which is also
            operated by {LEGAL_HOLDER} on Cloudflare.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>Clearing the browser's data for this site removes both.</p>

        <h2>Do Not Track</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing on this site tracks visitors across other sites. The site
          behaves the same with or without a Do Not Track or Global Privacy
          Control signal. There is nothing for the signal to turn off.
        </p>

        <h2>Correspondence</h2>
        <p>
          The subscription form on the home page enrolls an address in the
          Half-Built Robots mailing list. It is the same list the blog runs. The
          address goes to <a href="https://buttondown.com/">Buttondown</a>,
          which stores it and sends the mail. It is used for that list and
          nothing else. Enrollment is double opt-in, and every dispatch carries
          an unsubscribe link. The full terms are in the blog's
          <a href="https://www.half-built-robots.com/policies/mailing-list/"
            >mailing list policy</a
          >.
        </p>

        <h2>Retention</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Mailing list address.</strong> Held on the subscriber's
            consent until they unsubscribe.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Redemption shipping details.</strong> Held until delivery is
            confirmed, then deleted.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Cloudflare's logs and bot protection.</strong> Kept on
            Cloudflare's own schedule under
            <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
              >Cloudflare's privacy policy</a
            >.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Mail sent to the contact address.</strong> Used to answer
            the sender. Kept unless the sender asks for it to be deleted.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Where it is processed</h2>
        <p>
          The services named on this page are United States companies. Anything
          they hold for this site is processed in the US. Cloudflare takes part
          in the EU-US Data Privacy Framework.
        </p>

        <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
        <p>
          The site links to the Half-Built Robots blog and to other sites. Their
          privacy practices are their own. This policy covers this site only.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          This site is not directed at children under 13. It does not knowingly
          collect personal information from anyone under 13.
        </p>

        <h2>Your data</h2>
        <p>
          Anyone, wherever they live, may ask what this site holds about them.
          They may also ask for it to be corrected or deleted. Write to the
          contact address below. In nearly every case the site holds nothing.
          The records it can hold are a mailing list address and, while a
          redemption is in transit, a shipping address. The unsubscribe link in
          any dispatch removes the first.
        </p>
        <p>
          Anyone who believes a request was mishandled may complain to the data
          protection authority where they live.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>Revisions are posted on this page with a new date at the top.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <PolicyContact />
        <p>
          The email address is a Gmail account. Mail sent to it is also handled
          by Google under
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
            >Google's privacy policy</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
